+# Source-only M2 boredom-to-Play route V1
+
+Status: source-only formatted revision V2, not compiled or natively executed.
+Official rustfmt parsed/formatted all four Rust files and its check passed
+(edition 2021, skip_children=true). No Rust type checking is implied.
+This patch is an opt-in
+detached arithmetic candidate, not a world-host admission or an intervention in
+any existing organism. No seed, life, world, checkpoint, build target or native
+test was created or run. It does not establish useful play, relief, learning,
+ecological balance, GPU parity or production readiness.
+
+## Exact intervention
+
+Keep the pinned M2 recipe and recovery-confidence recipe unchanged. The existing
+source has 2,048 cells, M2 has 444, and the recovery extension has 16. New cells
+2508 and 2509 are a matched expression/common pair, giving 2,510 total cells.
+They never reuse M0's unrelated 2110 coordinate. Both have Identity activation,
+leak 1, bias 0, homeostatic gain 0, metabolic decay .01 and activity EMA decay .95.
+
+The declared phase order is 1, 2, **7**, 3, 4, 5, 6. Phase 7 runs after M2's
+raw/reference/opponent cells and before the existing five proposal ports. Its
+expression branch is the standard native dendrite:
+
+    q = 4*(a2095-a2097)
+        - 4*(a2055-a2057) - 4*(a2060-a2062) - 4*(a2065-a2067)
+        - 4*(a2085-a2087) - 4*(a2080-a2082)
+    b = tanh(max(q, 0))
+
+The implementation evaluates the manifest's individual products in their fixed
+order, rather than using the algebraic grouping above. The common branch has
+the same 12 source references and zero coefficients. Both branches use threshold
+0 and output gain 1, and both somas receive the identical offset, projection
+gain and local threshold through the same native kernel as the source. With
+leak 1 and homeostatic gain 0, their signed difference reflects this tick's
+expression, not persistent suppression after urgency resolves. EMA/metabolic
+banks still evolve and persist normally.
+
+Only exact observed Play action 213, Interact, Other, ObjectSlot, with its slot's
+features and an entity-plus-position target receives the two readout rows
+`+.25*a2508 - .25*a2509`. This enters the existing D component before its .25
+divisor, bounded paired ports and final integration. No post-policy probability
+correction, compulsory action or second source execution exists.
+
+The pair uses actual boredom axis 9/extension[0], not curiosity axis 5. Its
+inhibitors are positive-only fatigue, fear, pain, unsigned temperature stress
+and ATP **deficit**. ATP's base branch is reference-minus-availability, with
+reference .75. There is no ordinary-hunger veto. Actual biological boredom is
+never reduced or overwritten by this appendage. DriveSham replaces only the
+appendage drive inputs with references, as before; raw physiology stays present.
+
+The `.25` readout and `4` branch weights are provisional authored hypotheses,
+not measured biological calibration or equality with the M0 PlayV2 result.
+The API derives modulation using the actual `NeuralReceptorPhenotype` and
+`NeuralReceptorEffects::from_frame` path. The tests supply synthetic receptor
+frames and drive snapshots, not chemistry-generated ecological histories.
+
+## Identity and permissions of this API
+
+`M2BoredomDetachedCpuV1::fresh` accepts the existing strict genetic-only source
+admission, with Full or DriveSham core mode and Full or EqualWorkReadoutSham
+readout control. DirectSource is rejected. It does not import ordinary host,
+M0, M1, legacy M2 or existing-life state. Its outer envelope and both inner
+snapshots have new schemas and recipe identity. Old public restores still
+construct their original expected schemas and reject these snapshots, including
+an extracted inner snapshot. The new restore rejects an old inner envelope.
+Mode, control, generation, source hash/asset, dimensions, finite/bounded state
+and exact dendrites are checked before state is accepted.
+
+The old host source, its work counters, policy sampler, output identities and
+world-loop code are untouched. Shared private arithmetic gains an optional
+borrowed pair; old entry points pass None. Old recipes, dimensions and public
+state layouts do not change. Explicitly zero Play contributions do not add zero
+to old D values, preserving their bit patterns outside the new typed port.
+
+The new result exports source evaluation and separately identified native
+arithmetic receipts, **not old grouped sampled-action objects**. The old policy
+binding is used internally only to reuse group arithmetic. No new sampler,
+policy-gradient API, actor, waking plasticity or host dispatch is exposed. A
+separate typed policy/world-admission composition remains required before a
+world test. This avoids quietly admitting new scores under an old action owner.
+
+Binding validates Profile5, frame/slot features and the existing projector's
+slot-to-target and entity-to-slot consistency checks. Receipt provenance retains
+the tracked-object ID, exact target, observation slot, feature digest, frame
+digest and source generation. It cannot certify that a world entity is a toy,
+reachable, unowned or physically usable. Same-ID malformed Play fails closed;
+ordinary Other, Vocal, no-op and GRAB/same-target-release candidates gain no new
+row. A mask or missing compiled effector cannot manufacture an eligible action.
+
+## Parameters and work
+
+There are 816 fixed appendage synaptic/readout rows: the old 814 plus two Play
+readout rows. There are now 38 native branches, with 96 branch-input weights
+(old 72 plus 24). The new component has 40 explicit floating-point parameter
+scalars: 24 input weights, four branch threshold/gain values, ten soma-dynamics
+values and two readout weights. The activation enum and phase/address labels
+are not floating-point trainable parameters. All of these parameters are fixed.
+No source row, source optimizer coordinate or biological emitter changes.
+
+Per decision, in every control and whether Play is offered or absent, phase 7
+executes two soma updates, two assignments, two branches, 24 branch-input
+products and two readout products for each of 32 padded candidate slots.
+Additional semantic reservation is:
+
+    2*32 + 2*4 + 2*16 + 24*4 + 64*4 = 456 Q24
+
+Total appendage arithmetic is 27,344 + 1,016 + 4*common_Rest_source_products
++ 456 Q24. For 544 common products this is 30,992 Q24, with 462 appendage
+cell updates. Source work is additional and candidate-dependent as before.
+ReadoutSham executes the same pair and products with zero readout gates;
+DriveSham executes the same work at reference drive inputs. Group source
+readouts still execute once on the same already-computed source tape.
+Validation, sampling bookkeeping (internal only), serialization and diagnostic
+Jacobian construction retain the detached base's unpriced status. These are
+semantic units, not measured wall time, chemical ATP loss or a qualified host
+bill. No biological debit is applied by this detached evaluator.
+
+## Authored qualification gates, not results
+
+Six test functions in `confidence/boredom/tests.rs` cover:
+
+- Recipe bytes, counts, signed zero and finite/bounded new banks.
+- Boredom below/above .35 under the actual receptor projection; each urgency
+  input suppressing expression, subsequent recovery, preserved actual boredom
+  and no hunger-only or curiosity substitution.
+- Exact Play-only differences, ordinary Other/Vocal/GRAB/no-op isolation,
+  absent Play, equal-work readout sham and DriveSham.
+- Exact target/tracked provenance, malformed same-ID cases, Profile5-only
+  admission, changed-target stale rows, stale receptor tick, budget rejection
+  and unchanged state on rejected calls.
+- The same real source evaluation as the old route, old-state round-trip bytes,
+  source-once receipt, extra reservation, new warm/cold bytes, mode/control
+  rejection and opposite-identity restore rejection in both directions.
+- Full/readout-sham equal source/work, absent/present Play, and active Full
+  warm/cold continuation.
+
+Official rustfmt parse/format and formatting checks passed for V2. No compiler
+check, Clippy or native test has run on this patch. Source review and these
+source-only checks cannot establish compilation or
+passing runtime behavior. Existing legacy tests must also be rerun after
+approval on a released build lane, including the unchanged host checks.
+
+After explicit build-lane approval, a focused command is:
+
+    cargo test -p alife_training --features cpu-backend --lib cpu::motor_mediation::confidence::boredom::tests -- --test-threads=1
+
+This is a future command, not an execution record. Run formatting and strict
+Clippy and the full mediation/legacy-state regressions on the final same source.
+Do not point Cargo at an active frozen study checkout or reuse a live output
+directory. World admission and canonical novelty-aware physical tests are later
+gates, not authorized by the detached command above.
+
+## Biological interpretation and next decision
+
+Canonical grouped dispatch multiplies Play stimulation by `1 - actual
+interaction novelty`. A first unfamiliar toy interaction may investigate while
+delivering little play stimulation; later genuinely familiar interactions may
+deliver more. Direct toy-activation arithmetic must not be presented as relief
+from the canonical path. Physical failure gives no fabricated relief.
+
+Before choosing these weights, inspect the new component against source,
+innate, actual memory and cognitive components at admitted operating points.
+If .25 is negligible or saturates the existing D port, report that result and
+create a new named revision rather than silently tuning action selection.
+The target remains useful self-care with ordinary rest, satiation and no-ops,
+not perpetual action. Experiments 4/5/6 of
+https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/ motivate bounded edits,
+coherent wiring and measured iteration, but do not validate this controller.
